      "semantic_sha256": "7e842c974d720e27d813b6ecd11280ced0b0190b2c0ac8c838195c0f27c418ed"
    },
    {
      "body": "EVIDENCE. The added-to-basket pop-up shows the product price and a higher basket total including optional services; the FIN states that one or both paid services were pre-selected and automatically added to baskets unless consumers manually removed them.\nLEGAL REASONING. Regulation 40 treats this as an express-consent problem: consent to an additional payment cannot be inferred from a consumer failing to change a default option.\nSTATED LAW. Consumer Contracts Regulations 2013 Regulation 40; DMCC Act 2024 direct consumer-enforcement powers.",
      "container_path": "cases/uk_marks_electrical.json",
